## 7. Prometheus configuration for host-based routing

Prometheus is managed by the Prometheus Operator when installed using `kube-prometheus-stack`. Its URL/path settings belong in the Helm values that generate the Prometheus custom resource; do not make an ad-hoc edit to the generated StatefulSet as the long-term configuration method.

The two important fields are:

| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `prometheus.prometheusSpec.externalUrl` | The external URL Prometheus should advertise/use in generated links. |
| `prometheus.prometheusSpec.routePrefix` | The path prefix Prometheus serves on. |

The current lab uses the hostname at the root path, so the desired values are:

```yaml
prometheus:
  prometheusSpec:
    externalUrl: "http://prometheus.k3s.test"
    routePrefix: "/"
```

The external URL must match the actual address used by the browser:

- HostPort HTTP: `http://prometheus.k3s.test`
- NodePort HTTP: `http://prometheus.k3s.test:30143`
- HostPort HTTPS: `https://prometheus.k3s.test`

For host-based routing at `/`, do not leave an old URL such as `https://ddns.net` together with `routePrefix: /prometheus`.

### Inspect the live Prometheus custom resource

Your Prometheus custom resource name is:

```text
prometheus-stack-kube-prom-prometheus
```

Inspect the generated settings:

```bash
kubectl get prometheus prometheus-stack-kube-prom-prometheus \
  -n monitoring \
  -o jsonpath='ExternalURL: {.spec.externalUrl}{"\n"}RoutePrefix: {.spec.routePrefix}{"\n"}'
```

For the current HTTP HostPort lab, expected output is equivalent to:

```text
ExternalURL: http://prometheus.k3s.test
RoutePrefix: /
```

