## 12. Service exposure and the frontend NodePort

The frontend Service was previously:

```text
frontend-service   NodePort   ...   80:32000/TCP
```

Direct access to:

```text
http://10.227.142.162:32000
```

bypasses the NGINX Ingress Controller and reaches the frontend Service's NodePort directly.

When all application traffic is intended to enter through NGINX, application Services should normally be `ClusterIP` and not separately exposed with NodePort. After confirming that the Ingress route works, the frontend Service can be changed to ClusterIP:

```bash
kubectl patch svc frontend-service \
  -n app-ns \
  --type merge \
  -p '{"spec":{"type":"ClusterIP"}}'
```

Do this only when you no longer need direct NodePort access. Check the backend Service too:

```bash
kubectl get svc -n app-ns
```

NGINX can reach ClusterIP Services inside the cluster; clients outside the cluster do not need direct access to application NodePorts.

